WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:16.689 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  just from the title alone there are a  few things you can expect from a Tales  game a lengthy story melodramatic  writing dated visuals and of course a  real-time battle system for the most  part tales of verse area sticks to the  same formula the story is long and  punctuated with both predictable and  unexpected plot twists the writing can  swing from tender moments to  cringe-worthy ones and the real-time  combat is engaging but becomes stale  near the end where tales of Bruce area  differentiates itself from recent  entries is its mature story in  characters  [ __ ] demons velvet crow the  protagonist is introduced as a wholesome  young woman taking care of her younger  brother in a world overrun by demons  after her brother is sacrificed in order  to quell the evil in the world  velvet is transformed into a demon and  locked away in prison the opening hours  are slow but after they come to a close  tails of Bruce area quickly spirals into  a story of revenge when we revisit  velvet three years later she is no  longer the innocent wholesome girl from  the prologue she is angry what's  striking about velvet as opposed to past  tales protagonist is that she is driven  by rage and vengeance knock them back  that's an order  not  back or I'll eat you  now the darker tone makes up for tales  of verse areas slow first few hours  while the series has never shied away  from heavy themes it's refreshing to  play as a character in a Tales game  who's willing to do whatever it takes in  order to get what she wants she's not  afraid to kill steal and threaten when  it's necessary her apathy can get  exhausting at times even frustrating but  her motives are believable we'll take  this back to town and tell him you're  dead that should be enough to satisfy  the Exorcist and get them to call off  the search the same can be said about  the supporting cast of party members  however the standout character is  Eleanor unlike the rest of the team  Eleanor is virtuous she tries to help  people and do what she thinks is right  throughout most of the game she's at  odds with the company she keeps and  finds herself stuck between two very  different worlds  this foil creates an uneasy tension and  at times adds a much-needed reprieve  from Velvets cruelty no this is personal  once I regain my Exorcist powers  I vow to challenge you demon velvet the  other half of the experience comes in  the form of combat as expected the  trademark tails real-time battle system  returns but not without some changes  tales of Bruce area removes the  technical points bar and replaces it  with the soul gauge which is similar in  that it dictates how long you can chain  together combat and spell arts however  unlike in previous Tales games you can  steal Souls from your opponents by  knocking them out or stunning them the  soul gauge doesn't change the flow of  battle too much but it does add a bit  more fluidity to it the game offers a  wide variety of arts across all six  party members and as long as you have  enough souls you can chain any of them  together to create unique combos tales  games have always allowed for this kind  of experimentation but linking arts  hasn't felt this fluid or captivating  before once you get comfortable with the  combat you can keep the momentum of  battle going for minutes at a time  well that takes care of that but no  amount of experimentation can salvage  the repetitive nature of tales of Bruce  area the delight in unlocking new arts  fades about halfway through the game and  by then the battles become tedious near  the end I found myself focusing more on  avoiding enemies rather than trying  different characters or testing out new  arts this repetition extends to the  world and dungeon design like tales of  zestiria and tales of Xillia verse area  doesn't have an overworld instead you  travel from town to town by trekking  through large sectioned off areas which  could easily be confused with locations  from previous Tales games there isn't  much to do or see in these areas either  apart from fighting enemies and hunting  for treasure chests the dungeon design  is even worse dungeons consists of long  corridors that occasionally branch off  simple puzzles and dozens of similar  enemies apart from a palette swap these  multi-level dungeons look identical from  floor to floor textures and objects are  reused from corridor to corridor making  it a pain to navigate the puzzles don't  require much thought either in most  cases you flip a switch or light a torch  and the door opens it doesn't help that  tales of per serie looks dated at times  it's indistinguishable from 2013's tales  of Xillia the art direction can go a  long way at times to mitigate the poor  graphics especially in some later  dungeons but don't expect to be blown  away by it  demon blight has spread through the  village  do not fear with my power as an extra  system  I Artorius co-brand will end your pain  tales of Bruce areas weak presentation  until world design may be off-putting  but that only accounts for part of an  otherwise enjoyable tale the refined  combat in the darker tone paired with  the sinister characters makes for a more  engaging experience overall tales of  Bruce area may not reinvent the series  but it does take steps in an intriguing  new direction  [Music]

